00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:30.069
So to avoid the criticism that I know is coming,
I know people will write to me and say, David,

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:33.370
are you saying that these aren't nice things
people are doing or that we shouldn't applaud

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.370
them?

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:35.370
It's fine.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.340
People in bad situations, uh, should be doing
nice things and we should recognize that and

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.709
it's okay to do that.

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:45.269
Uh, but I read this example on Reddit, which
is a good one.

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:49.639
Someone gets caught in the rain and a random
stranger gives them an umbrella.

00:02:49.639 --> 00:02:50.639
That's nice.

00:02:50.639 --> 00:02:54.620
Rain was the problem and the umbrella was
the solution in that case.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:59.290
In a similar but slightly different example,
if a homeless person is caught in the rain

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:05.400
for years because they're persistently homeless
and society simply hasn't decided that we're

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.950
going to deal with that as an issue right
now and a passer by gives them an umbrella.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.689
Giving the numb under umbrella is still nice.

00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:17.219
But the problem in the second case is the
breakdown of our systems or the fact that

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:22.560
they don't exist even to begin with, to deal
with homelessness as a systemic problem.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.349
That's the difference here.

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:29.400
Friendly 80 year olds who are mowing lawns
for money, someone comes along and buys them

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.090
a better lawn mower.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.090
That's great.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.560
That's a nice thing to do.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:38.980
But why are so many people unable to retire
in our country and they have to keep working

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:44.930
including mowing lawns out in the heat at
age 80 that's really the problem.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:50.499
And the new lawn Mower, as nice as it might
be, doesn't actually solve the underlying

00:03:50.499 --> 00:03:51.499
problem.

00:03:51.499 --> 00:03:55.370
So cover the stories, that's fine, but talk
about structural issues and of course corporate

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.370
media won't.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.370
Why not?

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:02.419
Because corporate media has not only a bias
to sensationalism, but corporate media has

00:04:02.419 --> 00:04:08.939
a bias towards compartmentalized acute stories
that happen at one point in time rather than

00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:13.890
systemic issues that grow or change and shift
and are difficult to cover with a discreet

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.260
beginning, middle, and end.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:22.270
This is why if 30 people die in a terrorist
attack, that gets way more coverage than 10,000

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:28.260
starving African children dying because even
if you fix 50% of the starving African children

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:33.550
problem, there would still be 5,000 kids who
died that day instead of 10,000 and the story

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:34.830
becomes background.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:41.650
It doesn't have a discreet beginning, middle,
and end in the way that corporate news basically

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:46.450
requires in order to fill the format that
they've decided is the one that they're going

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.450
to carry out.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:53.220
So the the FOA, inspirational stories are
okay, as long as we point out what the systemic

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.100
problems are, corporate media is not going
to do that.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:56.680
So at least I'll do my best to do it for you.

